{"url": "https://lsa.umich.edu/math/graduates/Admissions.html", "final_url": "https://lsa.umich.edu/math/graduates/Admissions.html", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-30", "text": "Skip to Content\nU-M// LSA// Departments and Units// Majors and Minors// Look To Michigan// LSA Course Guide// LSA Gateway\nKeyword Search of math\nHome About Us People Centers & Outreach Seminars, Colloquia & Lectures News & Events\nfor\nUndergraduates Graduates Alumni & Friends Research\nSkip to Page Content\nGRADUATES ADMISSIONS\nGRADUATES\nAdmissions\nPh.D. Admissions\nM.S. Quantitative Finance & Risk Management\nM.S. Admissions\nAwards & Fellowships\nCourses\nPrograms\nRecent Ph.D. Recipients\nStudent Handbook - AIM & Math\nStudents On the Job Market - AIM & Math\nStudent Spotlight - AIM & Math\nThesis Defense Schedule\nAdmissions\nThe Fall 2027 application windows are now OPEN.\nPh.D. Admissions: Application deadline is December 15, 2026.\nM.S. Admissions: Application deadline is Februrary 1, 2027.\nWelcome to the University of Michigan Mathematics Graduate programs admissions webpage.\nThe Michigan Mathematics Department has consistently been ranked as one of the top ten Mathematics Departments in the country. For the 2026-2027 academic year, we have 155 Mathematics graduate students, of whom 46 are women or non-binary. Approximately 83% of graduate students are enrolled in the Ph.D. program. All of these students received support from the Department in the form of Graduate Student Instructorships, Graduate Student Research Assistantships, and fellowships.\nThe U-M Mathematics department offers 5 Master's degrees and 2 Ph.D. programs. Please use the \"Programs\" link at the left to explore our offerings.\nThe Michigan Mathematics Department also offers an MLB Scholars Program which is an enhanced option for the M.S. degree in either Mathematics or Applied and Interdisciplinary Mathematics for eligible students to give them professional knowledge of pure or applied mathematics in order to prepare to them for continuing toward a Ph.D.\nProgram Completion\nFrom 2001 - 2005, our AIM Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 71%. From 2006 - 2010, our AIM Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 82%. From 2011 - 2015, our AIM Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 76%. From 2016 - 2020, our AIM Ph.D. program has an 84% completion rate and 7% active students. The median time to degree for AIM Ph.D. students is 5.2 years.\nFrom 2001 - 2005, our Math Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 73%. From 2006 - 2010, our Math Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 83%. From 2011 - 2015, our Math Ph.D. program had a completion rate of 86%. From 2016 - 2020, our Math Ph.D. program has an 84% completion rate and 4% active students. The median time to degree for Math Ph.D. students is 5.5 years.\nFor the most up to date data, please see Rackham's interactive dashboard for Doctoral Program Statistics and Master's Program Statistics.\nMathematics\n2074 East Hall\n530 Church Street\nAnn Arbor, MI 48109-1043\nUndergraduate Students: math-undergrad-office@umich.edu\nGraduate Students: math-grad-office@umich.edu\nDepartment Administration: math-admin-office@umich.edu\nWebsite Updates: math-comm-web@umich.edu\nIntranet\nClick to call 734.764.0335\n734.764.0335\nSitemap\nInformation For\nProspective Students\nCurrent Students\nFaculty and Staff\nAlumni and Friends\nMore about LSA\nAbout LSA\nHow Do I Apply?\nNews\nLSA Magazine\nGive\nMaps\nStudent Resources\nCourses\nAcademic Advising\nMajors and Minors\nDepartments and Units\nGlobal Studies\nLSA Opportunity Hub\nConnect\nSocial Media\nUpdate Contact Info\nContact Us\nPrivacy Statement\nReport Feedback\n\u00a9 2026 Regents of the University of Michigan", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://lsa.umich.edu/math/graduates/Admissions.html#content"], ["U-M", "https://umich.edu/"], ["LSA", "https://lsa.umich.edu/"], ["Departments and Units", "https://lsa.umich.edu/lsa/academics/departments-and-units.html